# Command: SDD Health Check

Command: /sdd-health
Mode: AUDIT
Purpose: Validate SDDRA system integrity before execution

Description:
  Performs comprehensive health check of the .sdd/ system.
  Validates critical files, graph consistency, references,
  and token budgets. Reports status and recommendations.

Usage:
  /sdd-health
  /sdd-health --verbose
  /sdd-health --fix

Options:
  --verbose   Show detailed validation results
  --fix       Attempt to fix minor issues automatically

Checks:

  [H1] Critical Files Exist
      Files:
        - .sdd/PROJECT.sdd
        - .sdd/INDEX.sdd
        - .sdd/protocol/ROOT.sdd
        - .sdd/chains/graph.sdd
        - .sdd/templates/INDEX.sdd
      Action: FAIL if any missing
      Recovery: Restore from git or backup

  [H2] References Resolve
      Check: All @references in .sdd/ files resolve to existing files
      Action: WARN if unresolved reference
      Recovery: Create missing file or fix reference

  [H3] Graph Consistency
      Check: Chain graph has no orphaned nodes
      Check: All arms return to D0
      Check: No circular dependencies in non-cyclic parts
      Action: FAIL if graph is broken
      Recovery: Restore from backup

  [H4] Token Budgets Valid
      Check: All token budgets are positive numbers
      Check: Total budget < max_context
      Action: WARN if budget exceeds max_context
      Recovery: Adjust budgets or increase max_context

  [H5] Decision Ledger Valid
      Check: No duplicate DEC-IDs
      Check: All referenced decisions exist
      Check: Decision states are valid
      Action: WARN if issues found
      Recovery: Merge duplicates, fix references

  [H6] Template Index Valid
      Check: templates/INDEX.sdd exists
      Check: All template references resolve
      Check: No missing templates
      Action: WARN if templates missing
      Recovery: Restore from backup

  [H7] No Corrupted Files
      Check: All .sdd/ files are valid UTF-8
      Check: No truncated files
      Check: No binary files in .sdd/
      Action: WARN if corruption detected
      Recovery: Restore from git or backup

  [H8] State Consistency
      Check: No orphaned tasks
      Check: No conflicting states
      Check: State transitions are valid
      Action: WARN if inconsistencies found
      Recovery: Fix states manually or restore

Output:

  HEALTHY:
    All checks passed. System is ready for execution.

  DEGRADED:
    Non-critical issues found. System can execute with warnings.
    List: [warnings]

  UNHEALTHY:
    Critical issues found. Execution may fail.
    List: [errors]
    Recommendation: Fix issues before proceeding.

  FAILED:
    System is not operational.
    List: [critical errors]
    Recovery: Restore from backup or contact owner.

Exit Codes:
  0 - HEALTHY
  1 - DEGRADED
  2 - UNHEALTHY
  3 - FAILED

State: +
